Dump the real-workload per-node visit distribution.

DiskANN already counts node visits (_node_visit_counter, incremented in
cached_beam_search when _count_visited_nodes is set), but only enables counting
inside generate_cache_list_from_sample_queries, using its own internal sample
queries at L=15/beam=4 -- not the benchmark's actual query workload.

This patch re-enables counting after cache generation finishes, so the counter
accumulates over the real timed query set, and dumps it at teardown. That gives
the true access distribution, which is the object H(N) in the cost
decomposition: H(N) = (visits to the top-N nodes) / (total visits).

Two uses:
  - Recover the entire H(N) curve from ONE run, instead of one point per
    benchmark run.
  - Compare DiskANN's sample-based cache selection against the oracle ordering
    from real-workload visit counts, i.e. measure how much hit rate its
    selection heuristic leaves on the table.

CRITICAL correctness detail: generate_cache_list_from_sample_queries sorts
_node_visit_counter by descending count, after which position i no longer holds
node i. cached_beam_search increments _node_visit_counter[nbr.id], indexing by
node id, so the identity mapping MUST be restored before counting is re-enabled
or every visit is attributed to the wrong node. The patch rebuilds it.

Counting adds an atomic fetch_add per expanded node, so this perturbs timing.
Use it for distribution characterization only, never for a timed measurement.

Env-var gated by DISKANN_VISIT_TRACE=<path>; completely inert when unset.
Output is raw little-endian uint32 visit counts indexed by node id.

--- a/src/pq_flash_index.cpp
+++ b/src/pq_flash_index.cpp
@@ -9,6 +9,10 @@
 #include "pq_flash_index.h"
 #include "cosine_similarity.h"
 
+// ann-suite research instrumentation (env-var gated; see DISKANN_VISIT_TRACE below)
+#include <cstdlib>
+#include <fstream>
+
 #ifdef _WINDOWS
 #include "windows_aligned_file_reader.h"
 #else
@@ -57,6 +61,27 @@
 
 template <typename T, typename LabelT> PQFlashIndex<T, LabelT>::~PQFlashIndex()
 {
+    // --- ann-suite research instrumentation: dump real-workload visit counts ---
+    {
+        const char *ann_suite_trace = std::getenv("DISKANN_VISIT_TRACE");
+        if (ann_suite_trace != nullptr && ann_suite_trace[0] != '\0' &&
+            !this->_node_visit_counter.empty())
+        {
+            std::ofstream ann_suite_out(ann_suite_trace, std::ios::binary | std::ios::trunc);
+            uint64_t ann_suite_total = 0;
+            for (size_t vi = 0; vi < this->_node_visit_counter.size(); vi++)
+            {
+                uint32_t ann_suite_cnt = this->_node_visit_counter[vi].second;
+                ann_suite_total += ann_suite_cnt;
+                ann_suite_out.write((const char *)&ann_suite_cnt, sizeof(uint32_t));
+            }
+            ann_suite_out.close();
+            diskann::cout << "[ann-suite] visit_trace path=" << ann_suite_trace
+                          << " n_nodes=" << this->_node_visit_counter.size()
+                          << " total_visits=" << ann_suite_total << std::endl;
+        }
+    }
+
 #ifndef EXEC_ENV_OLS
     if (data != nullptr)
     {
@@ -343,6 +368,26 @@
     }
     this->_count_visited_nodes = false;
 
+    // --- ann-suite research instrumentation (env-var gated; inert when unset) ---
+    // The sort above ordered _node_visit_counter by descending count, so position i
+    // no longer corresponds to node i. cached_beam_search increments
+    // _node_visit_counter[nbr.id] -- indexed by node id -- so the identity mapping
+    // must be restored or every visit lands on the wrong node.
+    {
+        const char *ann_suite_trace = std::getenv("DISKANN_VISIT_TRACE");
+        if (ann_suite_trace != nullptr && ann_suite_trace[0] != '\0')
+        {
+            for (uint32_t vi = 0; vi < this->_node_visit_counter.size(); vi++)
+            {
+                this->_node_visit_counter[vi].first = vi;
+                this->_node_visit_counter[vi].second = 0;
+            }
+            this->_count_visited_nodes = true;
+            diskann::cout << "[ann-suite] visit tracing armed, dumping to "
+                          << ann_suite_trace << " at teardown" << std::endl;
+        }
+    }
+
     diskann::aligned_free(samples);
 }
 
